{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What? My debouncer can have dedicated devtools? Yep!"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Pacer ships devtools for watching and debugging every registered utility in real time. They run as a plugin inside the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" multi-panel UI."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The devtools are excluded from production builds by default, so they add nothing to your production bundle. See "},{"type":"link","href":"#production-builds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production builds"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if you need them in production."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the devtools packages for your framework:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/react-devtools @tanstack/react-pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"solid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/solid-devtools @tanstack/solid-pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"angular","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/angular-devtools @tanstack/angular-pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"svelte","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools @tanstack/svelte-pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/vue-devtools @tanstack/vue-pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"preact","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preact"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/preact-devtools @tanstack/preact-pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lit-alpine-ember-and-octane","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/devtools @tanstack/pacer-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These frameworks use the framework-independent Pacer plugin inside the TanStack Devtools dock."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic setup"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"react-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Your app content */}\n\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        eventBusConfig={{\n          debug: false,\n        }}\n        plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"solid-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/solid-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/solid-pacer-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Your app content */}\n\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        eventBusConfig={{\n          debug: false,\n        }}\n        plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"angular-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the plugin through the official "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provideTanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" provider in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"app.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". The provider creates the dock; you do not need to add a component to your template."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideTanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/angular-devtools/provider'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-pacer-devtools'\nimport type { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    ...(isDevMode()\n      ? [\n          provideTanStackDevtools(() => ({\n            plugins: [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()],\n          })),\n        ]\n      : []),\n  ],\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep your existing application providers alongside this provider."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"svelte-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the dock once in your root component. This example uses Vite's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import.meta.env.DEV"},{"type":"text","value":" flag to keep the dock out of production builds."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer-devtools'\n</script>\n\n{#if import.meta.env.DEV}\n  <TanStackDevtools plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n{/if}","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In SvelteKit, you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dev"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$app/environment"},{"type":"text","value":" as the condition instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vue-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer-devtools'\n\nconst dev = import.meta.env.DEV\nconst plugins = [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <AppContent />\n  <TanStackDevtools v-if=\"dev\" :plugins=\"plugins\" />\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Pacer panel appears alongside any other TanStack Devtools plugins you have installed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lit-alpine-ember-and-octane-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These frameworks use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsCore"},{"type":"text","value":" to mount the dock and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pacerDevtoolsPlugin()"},{"type":"text","value":" to add the Pacer panel. Mount one dock for your application and unmount it with the owning component."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a shared mount function. The following examples use Vite's development flag."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// devtools.ts\nimport { TanStackDevtoolsCore } from '@tanstack/devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/pacer-devtools'\n\nexport function mountDevtools() {\n  if (!import.meta.env.DEV) return () => {}\n\n  const target = document.createElement('div')\n  document.body.append(target)\n  const devtools = new TanStackDevtoolsCore({\n    plugins: [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()],\n  })\n  devtools.mount(target)\n\n  return () => {\n    devtools.unmount()\n    target.remove()\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"lit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connectedCallback"},{"type":"text","value":" and clean up in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disconnectedCallback"},{"type":"text","value":". This also supports removing and reconnecting the application element."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nclass App extends LitElement {\n  private cleanupDevtools?: () => void\n\n  override connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    this.cleanupDevtools = mountDevtools()\n  }\n\n  override disconnectedCallback() {\n    this.cleanupDevtools?.()\n    this.cleanupDevtools = undefined\n    super.disconnectedCallback()\n  }\n\n  override render() {\n    return html`<slot></slot>`\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('pacer-app', App)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"alpine","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpine"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the dock its own Alpine component so that it has one lifecycle owner."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Alpine from 'alpinejs'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nAlpine.data('devtools', () => {\n  let cleanup: (() => void) | undefined\n  return {\n    init() {\n      cleanup = mountDevtools()\n    },\n    destroy() {\n      cleanup?.()\n    },\n  }\n})\n\nAlpine.start()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<div x-data=\"devtools\"></div>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"ember","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ember"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount after rendering and register cleanup on the component. Check its lifecycle state because it can be destroyed before the scheduled callback runs."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport {\n  isDestroyed,\n  isDestroying,\n  registerDestructor,\n} from '@ember/destroyable'\nimport { scheduleOnce } from '@ember/runloop'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nexport default class App extends Component {\n  constructor(...args: ConstructorParameters<typeof Component>) {\n    super(...args)\n    if (import.meta.env.DEV) {\n      scheduleOnce('afterRender', this, this.mountDevtools)\n    }\n  }\n\n  private mountDevtools() {\n    if (isDestroyed(this) || isDestroying(this)) return\n    registerDestructor(this, mountDevtools())\n  }\n\n  <template>{{yield}}</template>\n}","lang":"gts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"octane","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount the dock in a layout effect and return its cleanup function. With Octane 0.1.36, keep application click and input events inside the Octane root. The dock uses Solid internally; both renderers use the same delegated event property names, which can otherwise invoke application handlers twice. The dock target created above is outside this boundary."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useLayoutEffect } from 'octane'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  useLayoutEffect(mountDevtools, [])\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      onClick={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\n      onInput={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\n    >\n      <AppContent />\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a Vite workspace example, keep Pacer's registry shared between the adapter and the devtools. Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/pacer"},{"type":"text","value":" as a direct dependency and use these optimization settings alongside your Octane plugin:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optimizeDeps: {\n  exclude: ['@tanstack/pacer'],\n  include: [\n    '@tanstack/devtools',\n    '@tanstack/pacer-devtools',\n    '@tanstack/octane-pacer > @tanstack/pacer > @tanstack/store',\n    '@tanstack/octane-pacer > @tanstack/pacer > @tanstack/devtools-event-client',\n  ],\n},","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./framework/octane/examples/useDebouncer","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane debouncer example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" includes this configuration and a live devtools plugin."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-builds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production builds"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default imports become no-ops in production builds:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// This is a no-op in production builds\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To debug a production issue with full devtools, switch to the production-specific imports:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// This includes full devtools even in production builds\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools/production'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registering-utilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registering utilities"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A utility only registers with the devtools when you give it a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":". Leave the option out and the instance stays out of the panels."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const debouncer = new Debouncer(myDebounceFn, {\n  key: 'My Debouncer', // friendly name shown in the devtools\n  wait: 1000,\n})","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"react","text":"React","level":3},{"id":"solid","text":"Solid","level":3},{"id":"angular","text":"Angular","level":3},{"id":"svelte","text":"Svelte","level":3},{"id":"vue","text":"Vue","level":3},{"id":"preact","text":"Preact","level":3},{"id":"lit-alpine-ember-and-octane","text":"Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane","level":3},{"id":"basic-setup","text":"Basic setup","level":2},{"id":"react-setup","text":"React setup","level":3},{"id":"solid-setup","text":"Solid setup","level":3},{"id":"angular-setup","text":"Angular setup","level":3},{"id":"svelte-setup","text":"Svelte setup","level":3},{"id":"vue-setup","text":"Vue setup","level":3},{"id":"lit-alpine-ember-and-octane-setup","text":"Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane setup","level":3},{"id":"lit","text":"Lit","level":4},{"id":"alpine","text":"Alpine","level":4},{"id":"ember","text":"Ember","level":4},{"id":"octane","text":"Octane","level":4},{"id":"production-builds","text":"Production builds","level":2},{"id":"registering-utilities","text":"Registering utilities","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhat? My debouncer can have dedicated devtools? Yep!\n\nTanStack Pacer ships devtools for watching and debugging every registered utility in real time. They run as a plugin inside the [TanStack Devtools](https://tanstack.com/devtools) multi-panel UI.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The devtools are excluded from production builds by default, so they add nothing to your production bundle. See [Production builds](#production-builds) if you need them in production.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall the devtools packages for your framework:\n\n### React\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/react-devtools @tanstack/react-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Solid\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/solid-devtools @tanstack/solid-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Angular\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-devtools @tanstack/angular-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Svelte\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools @tanstack/svelte-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Vue\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-devtools @tanstack/vue-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Preact\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/preact-devtools @tanstack/preact-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/devtools @tanstack/pacer-devtools\n```\n\nThese frameworks use the framework-independent Pacer plugin inside the TanStack Devtools dock.\n\n## Basic setup\n\n### React setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Your app content */}\n\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        eventBusConfig={{\n          debug: false,\n        }}\n        plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Solid setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/solid-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/solid-pacer-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Your app content */}\n\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        eventBusConfig={{\n          debug: false,\n        }}\n        plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Angular setup\n\nAdd the plugin through the official `provideTanStackDevtools` provider in `app.config.ts`. The provider creates the dock; you do not need to add a component to your template.\n\n```ts\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideTanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/angular-devtools/provider'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-pacer-devtools'\nimport type { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    ...(isDevMode()\n      ? [\n          provideTanStackDevtools(() => ({\n            plugins: [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()],\n          })),\n        ]\n      : []),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\nKeep your existing application providers alongside this provider.\n\n### Svelte setup\n\nAdd the dock once in your root component. This example uses Vite's `import.meta.env.DEV` flag to keep the dock out of production builds.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer-devtools'\n</script>\n\n{#if import.meta.env.DEV}\n  <TanStackDevtools plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n{/if}\n```\n\nIn SvelteKit, you can use `dev` from `$app/environment` as the condition instead.\n\n### Vue setup\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer-devtools'\n\nconst dev = import.meta.env.DEV\nconst plugins = [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <AppContent />\n  <TanStackDevtools v-if=\"dev\" :plugins=\"plugins\" />\n</template>\n```\n\nThe Pacer panel appears alongside any other TanStack Devtools plugins you have installed.\n\n### Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane setup\n\nThese frameworks use `TanStackDevtoolsCore` to mount the dock and `pacerDevtoolsPlugin()` to add the Pacer panel. Mount one dock for your application and unmount it with the owning component.\n\nCreate a shared mount function. The following examples use Vite's development flag.\n\n```ts\n// devtools.ts\nimport { TanStackDevtoolsCore } from '@tanstack/devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/pacer-devtools'\n\nexport function mountDevtools() {\n  if (!import.meta.env.DEV) return () => {}\n\n  const target = document.createElement('div')\n  document.body.append(target)\n  const devtools = new TanStackDevtoolsCore({\n    plugins: [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()],\n  })\n  devtools.mount(target)\n\n  return () => {\n    devtools.unmount()\n    target.remove()\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Lit\n\nMount in `connectedCallback` and clean up in `disconnectedCallback`. This also supports removing and reconnecting the application element.\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nclass App extends LitElement {\n  private cleanupDevtools?: () => void\n\n  override connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    this.cleanupDevtools = mountDevtools()\n  }\n\n  override disconnectedCallback() {\n    this.cleanupDevtools?.()\n    this.cleanupDevtools = undefined\n    super.disconnectedCallback()\n  }\n\n  override render() {\n    return html`<slot></slot>`\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('pacer-app', App)\n```\n\n#### Alpine\n\nGive the dock its own Alpine component so that it has one lifecycle owner.\n\n```ts\nimport Alpine from 'alpinejs'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nAlpine.data('devtools', () => {\n  let cleanup: (() => void) | undefined\n  return {\n    init() {\n      cleanup = mountDevtools()\n    },\n    destroy() {\n      cleanup?.()\n    },\n  }\n})\n\nAlpine.start()\n```\n\n```html\n<div x-data=\"devtools\"></div>\n```\n\n#### Ember\n\nMount after rendering and register cleanup on the component. Check its lifecycle state because it can be destroyed before the scheduled callback runs.\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport {\n  isDestroyed,\n  isDestroying,\n  registerDestructor,\n} from '@ember/destroyable'\nimport { scheduleOnce } from '@ember/runloop'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nexport default class App extends Component {\n  constructor(...args: ConstructorParameters<typeof Component>) {\n    super(...args)\n    if (import.meta.env.DEV) {\n      scheduleOnce('afterRender', this, this.mountDevtools)\n    }\n  }\n\n  private mountDevtools() {\n    if (isDestroyed(this) || isDestroying(this)) return\n    registerDestructor(this, mountDevtools())\n  }\n\n  <template>{{yield}}</template>\n}\n```\n\n#### Octane\n\nMount the dock in a layout effect and return its cleanup function. With Octane 0.1.36, keep application click and input events inside the Octane root. The dock uses Solid internally; both renderers use the same delegated event property names, which can otherwise invoke application handlers twice. The dock target created above is outside this boundary.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useLayoutEffect } from 'octane'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  useLayoutEffect(mountDevtools, [])\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      onClick={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\n      onInput={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\n    >\n      <AppContent />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFor a Vite workspace example, keep Pacer's registry shared between the adapter and the devtools. Add `@tanstack/pacer` as a direct dependency and use these optimization settings alongside your Octane plugin:\n\n```ts\noptimizeDeps: {\n  exclude: ['@tanstack/pacer'],\n  include: [\n    '@tanstack/devtools',\n    '@tanstack/pacer-devtools',\n    '@tanstack/octane-pacer > @tanstack/pacer > @tanstack/store',\n    '@tanstack/octane-pacer > @tanstack/pacer > @tanstack/devtools-event-client',\n  ],\n},\n```\n\nThe [Octane debouncer example](./framework/octane/examples/useDebouncer) includes this configuration and a live devtools plugin.\n\n## Production builds\n\nThe default imports become no-ops in production builds:\n\n```tsx\n// This is a no-op in production builds\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools'\n```\n\nTo debug a production issue with full devtools, switch to the production-specific imports:\n\n```tsx\n// This includes full devtools even in production builds\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools/production'\n```\n\n## Registering utilities\n\nA utility only registers with the devtools when you give it a `key`. Leave the option out and the instance stays out of the panels.\n\n```tsx\nconst debouncer = new Debouncer(myDebounceFn, {\n  key: 'My Debouncer', // friendly name shown in the devtools\n  wait: 1000,\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Devtools\nid: devtools\n---\n\nWhat? My debouncer can have dedicated devtools? Yep!\n\nTanStack Pacer ships devtools for watching and debugging every registered utility in real time. They run as a plugin inside the [TanStack Devtools](https://tanstack.com/devtools) multi-panel UI.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The devtools are excluded from production builds by default, so they add nothing to your production bundle. See [Production builds](#production-builds) if you need them in production.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall the devtools packages for your framework:\n\n### React\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/react-devtools @tanstack/react-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Solid\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/solid-devtools @tanstack/solid-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Angular\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-devtools @tanstack/angular-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Svelte\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools @tanstack/svelte-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Vue\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-devtools @tanstack/vue-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Preact\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/preact-devtools @tanstack/preact-pacer-devtools\n```\n\n### Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/devtools @tanstack/pacer-devtools\n```\n\nThese frameworks use the framework-independent Pacer plugin inside the TanStack Devtools dock.\n\n## Basic setup\n\n### React setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Your app content */}\n\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        eventBusConfig={{\n          debug: false,\n        }}\n        plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Solid setup\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/solid-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/solid-pacer-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Your app content */}\n\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        eventBusConfig={{\n          debug: false,\n        }}\n        plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Angular setup\n\nAdd the plugin through the official `provideTanStackDevtools` provider in `app.config.ts`. The provider creates the dock; you do not need to add a component to your template.\n\n```ts\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideTanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/angular-devtools/provider'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/angular-pacer-devtools'\nimport type { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    ...(isDevMode()\n      ? [\n          provideTanStackDevtools(() => ({\n            plugins: [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()],\n          })),\n        ]\n      : []),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\nKeep your existing application providers alongside this provider.\n\n### Svelte setup\n\nAdd the dock once in your root component. This example uses Vite's `import.meta.env.DEV` flag to keep the dock out of production builds.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-pacer-devtools'\n</script>\n\n{#if import.meta.env.DEV}\n  <TanStackDevtools plugins={[pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]} />\n{/if}\n```\n\nIn SvelteKit, you can use `dev` from `$app/environment` as the condition instead.\n\n### Vue setup\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer-devtools'\n\nconst dev = import.meta.env.DEV\nconst plugins = [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()]\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <AppContent />\n  <TanStackDevtools v-if=\"dev\" :plugins=\"plugins\" />\n</template>\n```\n\nThe Pacer panel appears alongside any other TanStack Devtools plugins you have installed.\n\n### Lit, Alpine, Ember, and Octane setup\n\nThese frameworks use `TanStackDevtoolsCore` to mount the dock and `pacerDevtoolsPlugin()` to add the Pacer panel. Mount one dock for your application and unmount it with the owning component.\n\nCreate a shared mount function. The following examples use Vite's development flag.\n\n```ts\n// devtools.ts\nimport { TanStackDevtoolsCore } from '@tanstack/devtools'\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/pacer-devtools'\n\nexport function mountDevtools() {\n  if (!import.meta.env.DEV) return () => {}\n\n  const target = document.createElement('div')\n  document.body.append(target)\n  const devtools = new TanStackDevtoolsCore({\n    plugins: [pacerDevtoolsPlugin()],\n  })\n  devtools.mount(target)\n\n  return () => {\n    devtools.unmount()\n    target.remove()\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Lit\n\nMount in `connectedCallback` and clean up in `disconnectedCallback`. This also supports removing and reconnecting the application element.\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nclass App extends LitElement {\n  private cleanupDevtools?: () => void\n\n  override connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    this.cleanupDevtools = mountDevtools()\n  }\n\n  override disconnectedCallback() {\n    this.cleanupDevtools?.()\n    this.cleanupDevtools = undefined\n    super.disconnectedCallback()\n  }\n\n  override render() {\n    return html`<slot></slot>`\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('pacer-app', App)\n```\n\n#### Alpine\n\nGive the dock its own Alpine component so that it has one lifecycle owner.\n\n```ts\nimport Alpine from 'alpinejs'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nAlpine.data('devtools', () => {\n  let cleanup: (() => void) | undefined\n  return {\n    init() {\n      cleanup = mountDevtools()\n    },\n    destroy() {\n      cleanup?.()\n    },\n  }\n})\n\nAlpine.start()\n```\n\n```html\n<div x-data=\"devtools\"></div>\n```\n\n#### Ember\n\nMount after rendering and register cleanup on the component. Check its lifecycle state because it can be destroyed before the scheduled callback runs.\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport {\n  isDestroyed,\n  isDestroying,\n  registerDestructor,\n} from '@ember/destroyable'\nimport { scheduleOnce } from '@ember/runloop'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nexport default class App extends Component {\n  constructor(...args: ConstructorParameters<typeof Component>) {\n    super(...args)\n    if (import.meta.env.DEV) {\n      scheduleOnce('afterRender', this, this.mountDevtools)\n    }\n  }\n\n  private mountDevtools() {\n    if (isDestroyed(this) || isDestroying(this)) return\n    registerDestructor(this, mountDevtools())\n  }\n\n  <template>{{yield}}</template>\n}\n```\n\n#### Octane\n\nMount the dock in a layout effect and return its cleanup function. With Octane 0.1.36, keep application click and input events inside the Octane root. The dock uses Solid internally; both renderers use the same delegated event property names, which can otherwise invoke application handlers twice. The dock target created above is outside this boundary.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useLayoutEffect } from 'octane'\nimport { mountDevtools } from './devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  useLayoutEffect(mountDevtools, [])\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      onClick={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\n      onInput={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\n    >\n      <AppContent />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFor a Vite workspace example, keep Pacer's registry shared between the adapter and the devtools. Add `@tanstack/pacer` as a direct dependency and use these optimization settings alongside your Octane plugin:\n\n```ts\noptimizeDeps: {\n  exclude: ['@tanstack/pacer'],\n  include: [\n    '@tanstack/devtools',\n    '@tanstack/pacer-devtools',\n    '@tanstack/octane-pacer > @tanstack/pacer > @tanstack/store',\n    '@tanstack/octane-pacer > @tanstack/pacer > @tanstack/devtools-event-client',\n  ],\n},\n```\n\nThe [Octane debouncer example](./framework/octane/examples/useDebouncer) includes this configuration and a live devtools plugin.\n\n## Production builds\n\nThe default imports become no-ops in production builds:\n\n```tsx\n// This is a no-op in production builds\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools'\n```\n\nTo debug a production issue with full devtools, switch to the production-specific imports:\n\n```tsx\n// This includes full devtools even in production builds\nimport { pacerDevtoolsPlugin } from '@tanstack/react-pacer-devtools/production'\n```\n\n## Registering utilities\n\nA utility only registers with the devtools when you give it a `key`. Leave the option out and the instance stays out of the panels.\n\n```tsx\nconst debouncer = new Debouncer(myDebounceFn, {\n  key: 'My Debouncer', // friendly name shown in the devtools\n  wait: 1000,\n})\n```\n"}
